# Cloudflare API token for cert-manager DNS-01 (letsencrypt ClusterIssuer).
#
# Applied out-of-band (like storage/proxmox-csi-plugin/configs). The real
# token is NOT committed — it lives in a gitignored file next to this one
# and is loaded into a Secret the ClusterIssuer references by name.
#
# 1. Create a Cloudflare API token: My Profile -> API Tokens -> Create Token
#    Permissions: Zone -> DNS -> Edit
#    Zone Resources: Include -> bluebirdforecast.com, tjzimmerman.com, tjzimmerman.dev
#
# 2. Save the token value into a gitignored file:
#      echo -n '<PASTE_TOKEN>' > public/cert-manager/configs/cloudflare-api-token
#
# 3. Create the Secret (key must be "api-token" to match clusterIssuer.yml):
#      kubectl create secret generic cloudflare-api-token \
#        -n cert-manager \
#        --from-file=api-token=public/cert-manager/configs/cloudflare-api-token
#
# cert-manager will then solve DNS-01 challenges and issue the gateway certs
# (istio-gateway ns: bluebird, personal-website).
